// What a mercenary waiting at the Sunken Lantern may carry, and what it asks
// to be hired. Every candidate is the one kind, `mercenary` in `monsters.ron`;
// what makes one unlike the next is its kit, drawn here, and its name, drawn
// from the `mercenary` set in `names.ron`. `src/mercenaries/` reads it.
//
// A band is the deepest floor the run has reached: nought on the first
// evening, before any floor, and ten once the throne's has been seen.
//
// Every field:
//   fee:     (base:, share_pct:), what a candidate asks: base, plus share_pct
//            percent of what everything in its kit is worth at its rolled level,
//            each thing priced as the adventurer would be told it, its kind and
//            its level both named, so a thing below nought is worth nothing
//   parts:   [(name:, chance:, rows:)], each rolled on its own, in this order:
//     name:    what the part is, as "weapon"; no two parts share one, and a
//              fourth part, a ring one time in ten, is a row here and no code
//     chance:  percent of candidates carrying one, 1 to 100
//     rows:    which one, drawn by weight among the rows at the band, as the
//              engine's spawn file reads them: [(item:, bands:, weight:, group:)]
//       item:    a name in `items.ron`
//       bands:   (first, last), both included, each from 0 to 10
//       weight:  how often against every other row of the part at the band,
//                above nought; only the ratio matters
//       group:   optional; (fewest, most) carried together; one when left out
//            A part with no row at the band is not carried.
//   levels:  [(bands:, level:, weight:)], how much better or worse than plain a
//            thing that takes levels is, drawn by weight among the rows at the
//            band and added to the least a found one of its kind is at uncursed:
//            nought for a weapon or armor. Below nought is cursed, as a thing
//            found below is. A thing that takes no levels draws none.
//     bands:   (first, last), both included, each from 0 to 10
//     level:   the level, below nought or not
//     weight:  how often against every other row at the band, above nought
(
    fee: (base: 80, share_pct: 100),
    parts: [
        (name: "weapon", chance: 100, rows: [
            (item: "dagger", bands: (0, 10), weight: 3),
            (item: "sword", bands: (0, 10), weight: 4),
            (item: "spear", bands: (0, 10), weight: 2),
            (item: "broadsword", bands: (3, 10), weight: 1),
        ]),
        (name: "armor", chance: 80, rows: [
            (item: "leather armor", bands: (0, 10), weight: 5),
            (item: "scale mail", bands: (0, 10), weight: 2),
            (item: "chain mail", bands: (3, 10), weight: 1),
        ]),
        (name: "consumable", chance: 50, rows: [
            (item: "potion of healing", bands: (0, 10), weight: 4),
            (item: "dart", bands: (0, 10), weight: 2, group: (4, 8)),
            (item: "javelin", bands: (0, 10), weight: 1, group: (2, 3)),
        ]),
    ],
    levels: [
        (bands: (0, 10), level: -1, weight: 2),
        (bands: (0, 10), level: 0, weight: 6),
        (bands: (0, 10), level: 1, weight: 2),
        (bands: (3, 10), level: 2, weight: 1),
    ],
)
